@startuml
title ADR-027 — Infrastructure scan and explicitly reviewed repair
autonumber
actor "PE / Admin" as User
control "Scheduler / API" as Trigger
control "InfrastructureDriftService" as Service
database "Repository / private artifacts" as DB
control "Environment operation + State lock" as Lock
boundary "Pinned Terraform runner" as TF
participant "Provider" as Provider
control "State service (UPDATE capability)" as State
Trigger -> Service: Scan acknowledged baseline
Service -> DB: Read original baseline/pins (missing => unavailable)
Service -> Lock: Claim Environment, then instance state lock
Service -> TF: Plan with refresh, private copied state and pinned inputs
TF -> Provider: Read actual infrastructure
TF --> Service: Complete private plan / drift / safe error
Service -> DB: Store safe findings; canonical state unchanged
Service -> Lock: Release only after process exit confirmed
User -> Trigger: Prepare repair(selected instances, scan)
Trigger -> Service: Generate exact repair review
Service -> Lock: Claim plan preparation
Service -> TF: Plan baseline; validate stable consumer outputs
TF --> Service: Saved plan, action set, private change digest
Service -> DB: Encrypted plan + expiring review token
Service -> Lock: Release after process stopped
Service --> User: Safe actions / blockers / expiry
User -> Trigger: Confirm review(token, requestId)
Trigger -> Service: Admit exact reviewed scope
Service -> Lock: Fresh owner + state locks
Service -> DB: Recheck baseline/state/dependency versions
note right of DB
Stable-output dependency acknowledgements use
exact original and latest encrypted baselines.
No consumer input/draft substitution.
end note
Service -> TF: Re-plan and compare full private changes
alt stale / destructive / unknown consumer impact
  Service --> User: Require new review / normal deploy; no apply
else equivalent in-place plan
  Service -> TF: Apply verified saved plan
  TF -> Provider: In-place update
  TF --> Service: Pulled state + validated stable outputs/inventory
  Service -> State: Acknowledge with original lock/fence, attempt and capability
  State -> DB: Persist encrypted state and successful baseline
  Service -> DB: Persist execution result; retain deployment history
end
Service -> Lock: Release only on confirmed terminal outcome
note over Service, Lock
Unknown process outcomes hold existing v2 locks.
No auto apply, orphan import or state refresh acceptance.
end note
note over DB
Owner-only bounded retention: scans 30d, private plans 24h.
Referenced audit and unresolved recovery evidence retained.
end note
@enduml
